1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,927
Look at this price tag. The price written on

2
00:00:02,927 --> 00:00:06,820
it is one thousand six hundred rupees. But that

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:09,800
sticker says six percent off, so the price you

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,451
pay is not the price on the tag. Three

5
00:00:12,451 --> 00:00:16,680
quantities are at work here. The first is the

6
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,400
marked price: the price written on the article, also

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,020
called the list price. The second is the discount:

8
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:27,477
the amount reduced, and the same idea is also

9
00:00:27,477 --> 00:00:30,920
called a rebate. The third is the selling price:

10
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:33,818
what is actually paid. One relation ties all three

11
00:00:33,818 --> 00:00:37,654
together: marked price minus discount equals selling price. And

12
00:00:37,654 --> 00:00:40,677
the tagged price never disappears, because the discount is

13
00:00:40,677 --> 00:00:44,611
always calculated from it, and never from the selling price.

14
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,940
The price tag has three parts, and each part

15
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:49,447
has a name. The marked price is the price

16
00:00:49,447 --> 00:00:52,424
written on the article; it is also called the

17
00:00:52,424 --> 00:00:54,987
list price, or the catalogue price. The discount is

18
00:00:54,987 --> 00:00:57,667
the amount that is reduced from that price, and

19
00:00:57,667 --> 00:01:00,787
the same idea is also called a rebate. The

20
00:01:00,787 --> 00:01:02,570
selling price is what is actually paid at the

21
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:06,419
counter. One relation ties the three together: marked price

22
00:01:06,419 --> 00:01:10,027
minus discount equals selling price. The tagged price never

23
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:13,423
disappears, because the discount is always calculated from the

24
00:01:13,423 --> 00:01:16,004
marked price. So keep the marked price on the

25
00:01:16,004 --> 00:01:18,458
board: the discount is only a part of it.

26
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:21,431
A book is marked eighty rupees, and the shop

27
00:01:21,431 --> 00:01:26,160
gives fifteen percent off. The marked price is the

28
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:29,135
whole bar: one hundred percent, that is eighty rupees.

29
00:01:29,135 --> 00:01:32,780
Step one is to find the discount, which is

30
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,964
fifteen percent of the marked price: fifteen over one

31
00:01:34,964 --> 00:01:38,000
hundred times eighty is twelve rupees. Step two is

32
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,419
the selling price: remove that discount from the marked

33
00:01:40,419 --> 00:01:42,102
price, so eighty minus twelve is sixty eight rupees.

34
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:45,367
You can see the fifteen percent block cut away

35
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:47,084
from the bar, and the selling price is what

36
00:01:47,084 --> 00:01:49,900
remains. So marked price minus discount equals selling price.

37
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:53,173
And the discount is always calculated on the marked

38
00:01:53,173 --> 00:01:56,660
price, never on the selling price, because the marked

39
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:58,891
price is the base for every discount.

40
00:01:59,533 --> 00:02:02,548
Now let us find a discount percentage. A bicycle

41
00:02:02,548 --> 00:02:04,725
is marked three thousand six hundred rupees, and it

42
00:02:04,725 --> 00:02:06,868
is sold for three thousand three hundred and twelve

43
00:02:06,868 --> 00:02:10,842
rupees. The difference between the two prices is two

44
00:02:10,842 --> 00:02:13,493
hundred and eighty eight rupees, and you can see

45
00:02:13,493 --> 00:02:15,213
that gap at the end of the bars. Now

46
00:02:15,213 --> 00:02:20,043
the discount percentage: its base is the marked price,

47
00:02:20,043 --> 00:02:23,733
never the selling price. The gap is measured against

48
00:02:23,733 --> 00:02:25,323
the whole bar, so the percentage is two hundred

49
00:02:25,323 --> 00:02:28,333
and eighty eight divided by three thousand six hundred,

50
00:02:28,333 --> 00:02:31,509
times one hundred. That is eight percent. Always divide

51
00:02:31,509 --> 00:02:34,404
by the marked price, and never by the selling price.

52
00:02:34,987 --> 00:02:38,707
Now the other direction: the discount percentage is given,

53
00:02:38,707 --> 00:02:41,106
and we must find the selling price. A ceiling

54
00:02:41,106 --> 00:02:42,789
fan is marked one thousand six hundred rupees, with

55
00:02:42,789 --> 00:02:46,485
six percent off. The discount is six percent of

56
00:02:46,485 --> 00:02:49,382
the marked price: six over one hundred times one

57
00:02:49,382 --> 00:02:51,760
thousand six hundred is ninety six rupees. The selling

58
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:54,611
price is the marked price minus the discount, so

59
00:02:54,611 --> 00:02:57,487
one thousand six hundred minus ninety six is one

60
00:02:57,487 --> 00:03:01,387
thousand five hundred and four rupees. Notice that the

61
00:03:01,387 --> 00:03:04,757
discount amount is ninety six rupees, while the discount

62
00:03:04,757 --> 00:03:07,107
rate is six percent. One is money, the other

63
00:03:07,107 --> 00:03:10,007
is a percentage of the marked price, so keep

64
00:03:10,007 --> 00:03:11,761
the amount in rupees and the rate in percent,

65
00:03:11,761 --> 00:03:14,418
and never mix the two up.

66
00:03:15,147 --> 00:03:17,130
There is a shortcut, and it comes from one

67
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:20,453
simple idea. If six percent is taken off the

68
00:03:20,453 --> 00:03:23,440
marked price, then ninety four percent is still payable.

69
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:29,399
Route one: find the discount first, ninety six rupees,

70
00:03:29,399 --> 00:03:33,947
and subtract it from one thousand six hundred. Route

71
00:03:33,947 --> 00:03:38,067
two: find the remaining percent first, ninety four percent,

72
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:40,162
and multiply it by one thousand six hundred. Both

73
00:03:40,162 --> 00:03:43,254
routes give one thousand five hundred and four rupees.

74
00:03:43,254 --> 00:03:45,020
So the shortcut is: selling price equals one hundred

75
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:48,087
minus d, over one hundred, times the marked price.

76
00:03:48,087 --> 00:03:50,817
Use whichever route you like, but check that the

77
00:03:50,817 --> 00:03:53,407
two routes agree. Two different routes are a free

78
00:03:53,407 --> 00:03:54,618
check on your answer.

79
00:03:55,127 --> 00:03:57,307
There are three questions you can be asked, and

80
00:03:57,307 --> 00:03:59,607
each one has its own route. If the marked

81
00:03:59,607 --> 00:04:01,638
price and the discount percentage are given, find the

82
00:04:01,638 --> 00:04:04,204
discount first, and then subtract it from the marked

83
00:04:04,204 --> 00:04:06,823
price. If the marked price and the selling price

84
00:04:06,823 --> 00:04:09,467
are given, find the discount by subtraction, and then

85
00:04:09,467 --> 00:04:11,881
divide that discount by the marked price, times one

86
00:04:11,881 --> 00:04:14,737
hundred. If the marked price and the discount amount

87
00:04:14,737 --> 00:04:16,947
are given, the selling price is simply marked price

88
00:04:16,947 --> 00:04:18,904
minus discount. In every case the first move is

89
00:04:18,904 --> 00:04:22,027
the same: find the discount, or find the marked

90
00:04:22,027 --> 00:04:25,407
price. And in every case the base for a

91
00:04:25,407 --> 00:04:27,992
percentage is the marked price. Read the question twice,

92
00:04:27,992 --> 00:04:32,938
and pick the route that fits the quantities you were given.

93
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,640
Now the mistakes that cost marks, and the fix

94
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,537
for each one. The first mistake is calculating the

95
00:04:35,537 --> 00:04:37,969
discount percentage on the selling price instead of the

96
00:04:37,969 --> 00:04:38,823
marked price. The second is adding the discount to

97
00:04:38,823 --> 00:04:39,984
the marked price, instead of subtracting it. The third

98
00:04:39,984 --> 00:04:41,072
is confusing the discount amount, ninety six rupees, with

99
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:43,580
the discount rate, six percent. The fourth is reading

100
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,715
fifteen percent off as if you pay fifteen percent,

101
00:04:44,715 --> 00:04:45,453
when eighty five percent is still payable. So check

102
00:04:45,453 --> 00:04:48,337
three things every time: the base is the marked

103
00:04:48,337 --> 00:04:49,387
price, the discount is subtracted, and the rate is

104
00:04:49,387 --> 00:04:50,590
a percentage while the amount is in rupees. Fix

105
00:04:50,590 --> 00:04:53,071
those four habits, and the marks stop leaking away.

106
00:04:53,753 --> 00:04:55,973
Before you write the answer, check that it makes

107
00:04:55,973 --> 00:04:59,009
sense. A discount always makes the selling price smaller

108
00:04:59,009 --> 00:05:01,253
than the marked price, so the selling price must

109
00:05:01,253 --> 00:05:02,753
be less than the marked price. And if d

110
00:05:02,753 --> 00:05:06,226
percent is taken off, then one hundred minus d

111
00:05:06,226 --> 00:05:09,513
percent is still payable. Here the marked price is

112
00:05:09,513 --> 00:05:12,793
one thousand six hundred rupees, and the selling price

113
00:05:12,793 --> 00:05:14,700
is one thousand five hundred and four rupees, which

114
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:18,157
is smaller. Six percent off leaves ninety four percent

115
00:05:18,157 --> 00:05:21,093
payable, and six plus ninety four is one hundred.

116
00:05:21,093 --> 00:05:24,786
So two checks every time: the selling price must

117
00:05:24,786 --> 00:05:26,463
be smaller than the marked price, and the two

118
00:05:26,463 --> 00:05:29,282
percentages must add up to one hundred. Write those

119
00:05:29,282 --> 00:05:33,004
two lines on your rough sheet before you answer.

120
00:05:33,587 --> 00:05:35,398
Your turn. Four quick checks. First: a shirt is

121
00:05:35,398 --> 00:05:38,867
marked four hundred and fifty rupees with seven percent

122
00:05:38,867 --> 00:05:41,661
off. Find the discount, and then the selling price.

123
00:05:41,661 --> 00:05:44,965
Second: an article is marked one thousand rupees and

124
00:05:44,965 --> 00:05:46,861
sold for nine hundred rupees. Find the discount, and

125
00:05:46,861 --> 00:05:50,032
then the discount percentage. Third: a table is marked

126
00:05:50,032 --> 00:05:53,607
two hundred and fifty rupees with five percent off.

127
00:05:53,607 --> 00:05:57,291
Find the selling price directly, using the percent that

128
00:05:57,291 --> 00:06:01,287
remains. And last: check that every selling price you

129
00:06:01,287 --> 00:06:03,347
write is smaller than its marked price. Take your

130
00:06:03,347 --> 00:06:07,218
time, and pause the video if you need to.

131
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,910
Let us check. For the shirt: seven percent of

132
00:06:20,910 --> 00:06:23,485
four hundred and fifty is thirty one rupees fifty,

133
00:06:23,485 --> 00:06:26,340
so the selling price is four hundred and fifty

134
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:29,029
minus thirty one fifty, which is four hundred and

135
00:06:29,029 --> 00:06:32,621
eighteen rupees fifty. For the article: the discount is

136
00:06:32,621 --> 00:06:34,972
one thousand minus nine hundred, that is one hundred

137
00:06:34,972 --> 00:06:38,380
rupees, and one hundred divided by one thousand, times

138
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:41,330
one hundred, is ten percent. For the table: five

139
00:06:41,330 --> 00:06:44,620
percent off leaves ninety five percent, and ninety five

140
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:46,564
over one hundred times two hundred and fifty is

141
00:06:46,564 --> 00:06:49,195
two hundred and thirty seven rupees fifty. And in

142
00:06:49,195 --> 00:06:52,224
all three the selling price is smaller than the

143
00:06:52,224 --> 00:06:56,100
marked price, and the base was the marked price.

144
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,940
Check both of those every time, and your answers

145
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:58,691
will be right.

146
00:06:59,513 --> 00:07:01,473
The whole chapter in four lines. One: the marked

147
00:07:01,473 --> 00:07:04,048
price is the price written on the article, and

148
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:07,403
the discount, or rebate, is calculated from it. Two:

149
00:07:07,403 --> 00:07:10,763
the selling price is what is actually paid, and

150
00:07:10,763 --> 00:07:15,273
selling price equals marked price minus discount. Three: the

151
00:07:15,273 --> 00:07:19,800
discount percentage is the discount divided by the marked

152
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:22,537
price, times one hundred. Four: the price flow is

153
00:07:22,537 --> 00:07:26,213
tag, reduce, pay, compare. So keep the marked price

154
00:07:26,213 --> 00:07:29,653
visible, subtract the discount, and check the answer against

155
00:07:29,653 --> 00:07:32,239
the tag. Thank you for watching, and see you

156
00:07:32,239 --> 00:07:33,564
in the next lesson.
